# What this service imports. Four lines, and everything else in
# requirements.txt is something one of these four brought with it.
#
#   fastapi           the framework, chosen in docs/plan/architecture.md
#                     section 2
#   uvicorn           the ASGI server that runs it
#   psycopg[binary]   the Postgres driver, version 3, with the wheel that
#                     carries libpq so the image installs no build tools
#   psycopg[pool]     the connection pool. The pool is load bearing rather than
#                     a performance choice: an identity set on a connection that
#                     is handed to the next request is the leak SET LOCAL exists
#                     to stop, and a service that opened a fresh connection every
#                     time could never demonstrate the difference
#   pyjwt[crypto]     offline signature checking of the access token, which is
#                     what the contract's memberToken scheme describes
#
# requirements.txt beside this file is the lock, and its first two lines are the
# command that regenerates it. Read docs/decisions/0012-python-dependencies.md
# before changing either.
fastapi
uvicorn
psycopg[binary,pool]
pyjwt[crypto]
